 › Explain this snippet.


 Here is the explanation:

 ╭─ rust ───────────────────╮
 │   fn main() {            │
 │       println!("hello"); │
 │   }                      │
 ╰──────────────────────────╯

 The main function is the program entry point. It calls println! which writes to stdout. This is
 very idiomatic Rust and the canonical hello-world example.











